The DNA in one cell contains enough information to reconstruct
you just as you were on the day you were born, but would this
really be you? I don't know, maybe, but nobody really knows. The
individual atoms in your body would be different but that is not
important as we change our atoms many times in a lifetime, so
that can have nothing to do with identity. What is important is
our memories and they would be gone, a severe disadvantage. But
how severe?
  
Am I the same man I was a hour ago or a day ago; yes even though
my memories are slightly different. Am I the same man I was 10
years ago; pretty much although I've changed a lot (I used to be
a liberal). Am I the same man I was when I was 3; unclear, I
have only a few vague memories of that time. Am I the same man I
was on the day I was  born?
 
